,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kwakum language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwakum_language,"Kwakum is classified as belonging to the Bantu subgroup A90 of the Zone “A” Bantu languages, and specifically labelled A91 by Guthrie. According to one of the newest updates to the Bantu classification system, other languages belonging to this subgroup are: Pol, Pɔmɔ, Kweso and Kakɔ.",Kwakum,Niger-Congo
1,Nigersko-kongoanski jezici – Wikipedija / Википедија,https://sh.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigersko-kongoanski_jezici,"Niger-kongoanski jezici su poznati po svom sistemu imeničkih klasa. Ovi sistemi su slični sistemu gramatičkog roda u drugim jezicima. Često ih ima više od desetak, a odnose se na muškarce, žene, živa bića, predmete, biljke, lokacije, grupe objekata itd.",Kwakum,Niger-Congo
2,Kwakum Language (KWU) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kwu/,Kwakum is a stable indigenous language of Cameroon. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family.,Kwakum,Niger-Congo
